  "Bug_Title": "PERM: Custom class loader does not call its superclass\u2019s getPermissions() (PERM_SUPER_NOT_CALLED_IN_GETPERMISSIONS)\uf0c1",
  "Bug_Details": "\nSEI CERT rule SEC07-J requires that custom class loaders must always call their superclass's getPermissions()\nmethod in their own getPermissions() method to initialize the object they return at the end. Omitting it means\nthat a class defined using this custom class loader has permissions that are completely independent of those\nspecified in the systemwide policy file. In effect, the class's permissions override them.\n",
  "Bug_Explanation": "The bug is in the overriding of getPermissions method in MyClassLoader class. The superclass's getPermissions() method is not called, meaning that the class's permissions are not initialized and can be overridden by the systemwide policy.",
